# Repository-wide line ending policy: text files are stored with LF and
# checked out with LF on every host, so tools that read committed sources
# (gofmt, tests matching component source) behave the same on Linux, macOS and
# Windows. Attributes override each developer's core.autocrlf, so no local Git
# configuration is required; CONTRIBUTING.md documents how to refresh a checkout
# created before this rule landed. Shell scripts are covered by this rule too:
# they run inside Linux containers and must stay LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored assets: no conversion, no textual diff, no three-way merge.
*.bcmap binary
*.pfb binary
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary

# Preserve upstream license bytes (including their original whitespace).
# Exact paths only: source files and other vendored files retain normal checks.
frontend/public/fonts/rare-han/OFL.txt -whitespace
frontend/public/pdfjs/cmaps/LICENSE -whitespace
frontend/public/pdfjs/standard_fonts/LICENSE_LIBERATION -whitespace
